From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] meson: phoenix backend -- the optional ioctl()
 interposer

phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_ioctl.c answers the Linux sync_file ioctls
(SYNC_IOC_MERGE, SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO) on the backend's in-process sync
files for programs linked with -Wl,--wrap=ioctl (Mesa's libsync merges
sync files with raw ioctl()s). Its own archive member, like
drm_phoenix_wrap.c: a program linked without --wrap=ioctl never pulls it.
---
 meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -257,6 +257,7 @@ if host_machine.system() == 'phoenix'
     'phoenix/xf86drm_phoenix.c', 'phoenix/drm_phoenix_kms.c',
     'phoenix/drm_phoenix_v3d.c', 'phoenix/drm_phoenix_logic.c',
     'phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap.c',
+    'phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_ioctl.c',
   )
   inc_phoenix = [include_directories('phoenix')]
 endif
